From 51f11121394c990772003170b9dda6fdd4c6b27d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: danishistired <iamdanishverma@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:30:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] blt-toasty: notify Slack when Toasty finishes triage (#35)

Maintainers had no signal when Toasty triaged or quarantined an issue.
Add a Workers-native Slack notifier (js fetch + env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL,
no urllib/os.getenv) and wire it into the two places triage ends:

- detect_duplicates, the last pipeline stage, on both exit paths, with
  the confirmed duplicate candidates and their similarity scores;
- quarantine_event, when env is available. redact() now passes env
  through so PII-gate quarantines are reported too.

The Block Kit message carries the issue number/link, CWE ids and labels,
a severity tier derived from the CWEs, quarantine status with a fixed
reason category, and duplicate findings. It never includes the title,
report text, summary or the raw quarantine reason, so unredacted text
cannot reach Slack. Delivery is best effort: unset webhook skips, and
errors are logged and swallowed so triage never fails because of Slack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
